<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Win Myint</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">born 1951</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Win Myint is a Myanmar politician of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-league-for-democracy">National League for Democracy</a> who was president from March 2018 until the military coup of 1 February 2021. A lawyer and former political prisoner, he had served as speaker of the lower house of parliament. He was arrested with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aung-san-suu-kyi">Aung San Suu Kyi</a> during the coup and later sentenced to prison by the junta.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/win-myint.jpg" alt="Win Myint" width="320" height="462" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Roman Kubanskiy (creator of composite from two sources above) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Myanmar_President_Win_Myint.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
